      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5cae645ea7ac1f18dd7e006e",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 17
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "100% support. Games like Warframe do this, first giving you a notification and a fun bite sized summary of the update. The community in that game actually gets pretty hyped about seeing the \"Red Text\" notifications appearing in their chat. The majority of the VRC community never check patch notes or even know updates have happened until friends tell them, and the first things they get told are what's broken, not what's new or fixed. It also causes substantial misinformation and confusion. I feel like it actually contributes quite a bit to the undue negativity updates often carry.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
